# Catalog vs customer templates

Two layers. Do not mix them up.

## Catalog (`/catalog`)

- Source of truth: `apps/web/app/catalog/templates.ts` plus thumbs in `apps/web/public/catalog/`
- Adding a catalog card is one list item + a thumb. Do not add a CSS file per card on the index
- Preview pages live at `/catalog/[slug]` only after they are built. Live so far: `/catalog/barber`, `/catalog/hairdresser`, `/catalog/nailtech`, `/catalog/makeup`, `/catalog/massage`, `/catalog/home-pricing`, `/catalog/industrial`, `/catalog/dressmaker`, `/catalog/trainer`, `/catalog/photographer`, `/catalog/event-planner`
- Set `href` on a template when its preview exists. Until then the card CTA stays WhatsApp
- Previews are demos of the master (e.g. Island Cuts), not live customer shops

## Customer sites (not built)

- Live masters are hardcoded HTML under `apps/harricom/` (`barber/`, `cook-shop/`, etc.)
- Today a launch is copy the folder and swap name, photos, prices, WhatsApp by hand
- There is no clone step: no customer records, no “drop in their pics and generate”

## When asked to clone later

Keep this split:

1. Master template — layout, brand, WhatsApp booking (one per trade, stays in the repo)
2. Customer record — name, parish, prices, photos, WhatsApp
3. Build — render (1)+(2) onto the customer’s domain

Do not start (2) or (3) until Patrick asks. Until then, keep the catalog list cheap to extend and leave HTML masters as copy-paste.
